note:
R102 - gen7 EB (0x00000400) archive layout constraints a member RENAME would meet (review 2026-09-25 R97-R101 F1). Measured per
archive on the six trees R99 inspected (X360 / PS3 Legacy, X360 / PS3 NHL 15, PS3 NHL 12 / 13 - four distinct titles). Read-only.

Header (EB): 0x04 file_count | 0x08 version | 0x0C name_table_offset | 0x10 word_10 (unknown) | 0x14 u8 name_slot | 0x15 u8 dir_slot |
0x16 u16 dir_count | 0x18 u64 archive_size | rows at 0x30 (16 B) | name table at name_table_offset: file_count x name_slot bytes, each
`u16 dir index | basename NUL-padded` | dir table at align16(name end): dir_count x dir_slot bytes.
Per archive:
  L1 row order: rows non-decreasing by path_hash? by full path? by (dir, basename)? - which one the stored order follows;
  L2 name slot: name_slot, max(2 + len(basename) + 1) over rows, headroom bytes; count of team-art basenames (R99 families) whose art id
     field could grow by 1 / 2 / 3 digits and still fit;
  L3 hash collisions: distinct paths sharing a path_hash inside the archive (and across the tree's archives);
  L4 tables: name table end, dir table start / end, first payload offset (min block << 4), gap bytes and whether they are zero;
     archive_size vs file length vs last entry end; word_10 relations tried (name_end, dir_end, first payload, file_count*name_slot ...);
  L5 destination occupancy in the team-art namespace (per tree, across archives): for each family and id, the member exists?
     - output = the set of ids with members per family, so a proposed b can be checked; plus the count of ids 0..1023 free in EVERY
     family (a candidate destination pool) - occupancy only, not a support claim.
Usage: python r102_eb_layout_constraints.py <out.json>
